r Band-&quot;Abracadabra&quot;<br /> <b>Wraith: The Oblivion: </b>Kansas-&quot;Dust in the Wind&quot;<br /> <b>Changeling: The Dreaming: </b>\u200bThe Wolfe Tones-&quot;Fairy Hills&quot;<br /> <b>\u200bHunter: The Reckoning: </b>Black Sabbath-&quot;Paranoid&quot;<br /> <b>Mummy: The Resurrection: </b>\u200bThe Kossoy Sisters-&quot;I'll Fly Away&quot;<br /> <b>\u200bStreet Fighter: The Storytelling Game: </b>\u200bCarl Douglas-&quot;Kung Fu Fighting&quot;<br /> <b>\u200bSenshi: The Merchandising: </b>\u200bP. Egoist-&quot;Sailor Scouting (Sailor Moon Rap)&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:32:38-08:00","id":1053531,"title":"","content":"I'll toss in Rasputina's &quot;Thanks For the Ether&quot;, as well as &quot;The Lost &amp; Found&quot; (which has a really good cover version of CCR's Bad Moon Rising)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:55:34-08:00","id":1053543,"title":"","content":"Any sabbat game is immediately improved with the proper application of Slayer albums","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T19:36:11-08:00","id":1054157,"title":"","content":"For vampire the masquerade nothing is better to me than Bloodsucker 2000 by Paralysed age.<br /> <br /> For werewolf <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c0trGRJs_IU\" data-code=\"c0trGRJs_IU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/c0trGRJs_IU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:42:20-08:00","id":1055707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1049085-albums-for-darkness?p=1053518#post1053518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had to pick a theme for each gameline, here would be my picks. I avoided KOTE and Demon because I don't use those gamelines. I did include Street Fighter and the fan game Senshi: The Merchandising though.<br /> <br /> <b>\u200bWerewolf: The Apocalypse: </b>\u200bMayhem-&quot;Freezing Moon&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting choice. While I'm not a W:tA player, it never stuck me as the game where Freezing Moon would be appropriate (wolf analogies not withstanding). Why did you choose that one?<br /> <br /> Might I suggest Nattens Madrigal for the beauty covered in rawness aspect, or something from WittR (I will lay down my bones...) for the serenity in nature aspect?<br /> <br /> Also, apologies for the tangent, but debating the myriad facets of Black Metal is a hobby of mine.<br /> <br /> The perfect background of a vaudlerie-filled Sabbat hell ride would be, for me either Folkfuck Folie from Peste Noire, or something from the newer Darkthrone albums. Unlike fast, meet final death young, and leave a good pile of ashes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:03:57-08:00","id":1055884,"title":"","content":"i cant stop thinking on The Pixies for some elements of world of darkness.. am i the only one who belives they provide a very interesting soundtrack for a Cultist of Ectasy/Orphan game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pa